David Zykin (zykin@noc.usfca.edu) wrote:
: I've been looking for a disk optimizer that will defragment my disks 
: without my having to get the users off them. The users get annoyed at 
: being asked to get off the system for any reason at all, and not wishing 
: to incur their displeasure I asked around. A DEC tech support person 
: mentioned PolyCenter File Optimizer for OPENVMS. He said I could use it 
: with the users on the system. This would certainly satisfy my political 
: requirements, if its true.

: Has anyone else used this product, or something like it? I'd like to get 
: some opinions before I approach the boss about buying it.

I don't think there is a utility that will allow optimizing index files, 
while they are open.  You could create a command procedure that converts 
your files every night (when all your users are gone) and, to create an 
optimized .FDL (every week, depending on the file's usage).

I believe Touch Technology markets a RMS tuning tool, but don't think it 
works when file is being accessed by other processes.

For disk maintenance, we use DISKEEPER.  This tool, we use with users 
online, and suffer no noticeable performance penalty.

Hope that helps.
